cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the derived catalogue, please cite the paper and this repository."
title: "Identifiability diagnostics for ground-based asteroid lightcurves"
abstract: >-
  A priori identifiability diagnostics for asteroid rotation periods observed
  from the ground with nightly photometric zero points: the P vs P/2 flip
  threshold, the minimum identifiable amplitude, the population flip risk, and a
  nested P vs 2P test with matched controls, held-out validation, a
  higher-harmonic control and a real-data positive control. Version 1.2.0
  fixes the calibration noise defect of v1.1.1 and supersedes v1.1.1 and v1.0.0.
